obs MY OWN HOT PASS CAUGHT ME FOUR TIMES, AND ONE OF THEM IS THE LAP'S OWN SUBJECT. I cited %535 and %536 by NUMBER on the operator card -- two unshared citations above the spine's shared_max of 534 -- in the very lap whose whole subject is rule 4, cite by stamp until the row is shared. The guard read it in 29s and both now spell their stamps. The other three were as mechanical: the ledger headline still said 534 where the spine measured 536, and reds_ledger_monotone read the same drift from the other side; and my new landed-accounts shelf carried two links at the CARD's depth, because I folded a card block one directory down and copied its relative paths with it.
obs AND THE SAME FOLD FAULT WAS ALREADY STANDING IN A PEER'S SHELF. fold_shelf_link went red between my cold and hot passes -- not from my edit but from the round-open pulling in construction/archive/20260907-013015_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, whose fold carried three links at the card's depth in exactly the shape mine did. Five lost links, two mine and three that ship's. I repaired all five, each under the single correction the scan itself prints. Worth a peer's eye: the fold that writes a landed-accounts shelf does not re-anchor the block's links the way tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh does for a REDS row, and two ships made the identical mistake within an hour.
